# L §5.16 Closed forms: "mean(e), e a sum of known multiples of random facts plus a known constant: the same sum of
# their means"; the table's mean is the one a closed form reads (round 18, C1-47). The table: normal(m, s) mean m = 5;
# uniform(a, b) (a + b)/2 = 3; exponential(rate) 1/rate = 4; gamma(shape, scale) shape · scale = 6; poisson(mean) = 3;
# binomial(n, p) n·p = 10 × 0.3 = 3; negbin(mean, size) = 2.5. (Was L5_16_mean_of_dist_value's q1, on distribution
# values, now refused.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input gn: dist
input gu: dist
input ge: dist
input gg: dist
input gp: dist
input gb: dist
input gnb: dist

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  gn = normal(5, 2) to 0.01
  gu = uniform(2, 4) to 0.01
  ge = exponential(0.25) to 0.01
  gg = gamma(2, 3) to 0.01
  gp = poisson(3)
  gb = binomial(10, 0.3)
  gnb = negbin(2.5, 3)

ask q1: mean(gn), mean(gu), mean(ge), mean(gg), mean(gp), mean(gb), mean(gnb)
=== expect
q1: (5 (horizon none), 3 (horizon none), 4 (horizon none), 6 (horizon none), 3 (horizon none), 3 (horizon none), 2.5 (horizon none))
  cut 2026-12-31
